  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape in late August 2026 is defined by a deep interplay between regulatory restructuring and architectural evolution. Bipartisan momentum behind the CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633) continues to set the standard for institutional compliance, establishing guardrails that bridge traditional finance and digital assets. Meanwhile, institutional engagement with spot Bitcoin assets has matured into a steady-state macro-allocation strategy. Technologically, the landscape is witnessing a fascinating rivalry: Ethereum maintains robust EVM dominance, but Bitcoin-native execution layers\u2014empowered by languages like Clarity and modular execution frameworks\u2014are steadily bringing deterministic smart contracts to the world's premier store of value. Concurrently, the transition toward non-custodial cross-chain liquidity and direct verification models is mitigating the systemic risks previously introduced by vulnerable legacy bridges.",
